Z||000003||Steve Normington||07-12-2001||01:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DecadenceR:<BR><B>* Your computer won't work unless it has it's own AC blowing on it. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>This happened at work last week. For two days, I couldn't log onto PFF from work.<P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>* Hot air balloons can't go up, because the air outside is hotter than the air inside. <P>* Airplanes can't land because the asphalt is too soft. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This actually happens in Arizona. The aircraft manufacturers didn't provide a weight and temperature chart that went above 120 Deg F, so the planes couldn't take off.<BR>||||reg||1
